Enable the Jetson Nano eMMC module's eMMC and pin it to mmc0

GoSD's jetson-nano board targets the 16GB eMMC production module
(P3448-0002), but mainline only describes the SD-card developer kit:
tegra210-p3450-0000.dts is a P3448-0000 module, which has no eMMC, on a
P3449 carrier. Booted on the eMMC module, that DTB leaves SDMMC4 disabled,
so the eMMC never appears and gosd-init cannot find its boot partition in
NVIDIA's APP partition (bean gosd-wxy7).

This patch makes four changes:

- SDMMC4 (mmc@700b0600), the eMMC, is enabled with an 8-bit bus and marked
  non-removable, exactly as mainline enables the eMMC on the Jetson TX1
  module (tegra210-p2180.dtsi). Its supplies are the rails NVIDIA's L4T
  power tree for the P3448 module gives SDMMC4: vqmmc from the MAX77620's
  SD3 (max77620_sd3, 1.8 V; vdd_1v8 here) and vmmc from p3448_vdd_3v3_sys
  (vdd_3v3_sys here). Speed modes are left as tegra210.dtsi's SDMMC4 node
  declares them: mmc-hs400-1_8v with its dqs-trim and pad calibration,
  which is what the TX1 runs on. NVIDIA's DTS also runs this module's eMMC
  at HS400, with enhanced strobe on top; no mainline Tegra210 DTS enables
  enhanced strobe, so it is left out.
- SDMMC1 (mmc@700b0000) is disabled. It is the microSD slot on the
  P3448-0000 module, and NVIDIA's DTS for the eMMC module disables it.
- SDMMC3 (mmc@700b0400) is disabled. Mainline enabled it for SDIO cards in
  the P3449 carrier's M.2 Key E slot (commit 1f32a31fe27e); NVIDIA's DTS
  leaves it disabled on this module, and GoSD's kernel builds no WLAN
  drivers.
- An mmc0 alias pins the eMMC to mmc0. mmcblk device names follow the host
  index (drivers/mmc/core/block.c), so NVIDIA's APP partition is always
  /dev/mmcblk0p1, gosd-init's first boot-partition candidate.

Sources:
- Linux v6.18.60: arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra210.dtsi,
  tegra210-p2180.dtsi and tegra210-p3450-0000.dts.
- NVIDIA L4T R32.7.6's device trees, as mirrored by OE4T
  (github.com/OE4T/linux-tegra-4.9, branch oe4t-patches-l4t-r32.7.6, under
  nvidia/platform/t210/porg/kernel-dts/): tegra210-p3448-0002-p3449-0000-b00.dts,
  tegra210-porg-p3448-common.dtsi and
  porg-platforms/tegra210-porg-power-tree-p3448-0000-a00.dtsi.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra210-p3450-0000.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra210-p3450-0000.dts
@@ -13,6 +13,12 @@
 
 	aliases {
 		ethernet = "/pcie@1003000/pci@2,0/ethernet@0,0";
+		/*
+		 * GoSD (github.com/jphastings/gosd): pins the eMMC to mmc0 so
+		 * it is always /dev/mmcblk0 and NVIDIA's APP partition, which
+		 * holds GoSD's boot partition, is /dev/mmcblk0p1.
+		 */
+		mmc0 = "/mmc@700b0600";
 		rtc0 = "/i2c@7000d000/pmic@3c";
 		rtc1 = "/rtc@7000e000";
 		serial0 = &uarta;
@@ -554,7 +560,13 @@
 	};
 
 	mmc@700b0000 {
-		status = "okay";
+		/*
+		 * GoSD (github.com/jphastings/gosd): SDMMC1 is the microSD slot
+		 * on the dev kit's P3448-0000 module. The eMMC module
+		 * (P3448-0002) GoSD targets has no slot, and NVIDIA's own
+		 * tegra210-p3448-0002-p3449-0000-b00.dts disables it too.
+		 */
+		status = "disabled";
 		bus-width = <4>;
 
 		cd-gpios = <&gpio TEGRA_GPIO(Z, 1) GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
@@ -565,7 +577,14 @@
 	};
 
 	mmc@700b0400 {
-		status = "okay";
+		/*
+		 * GoSD (github.com/jphastings/gosd): SDMMC3 is SDIO to the
+		 * P3449 carrier's M.2 Key E slot (mainline commit
+		 * 1f32a31fe27e). It belongs to that carrier, not the module:
+		 * NVIDIA's DTS for the eMMC module leaves it disabled, and
+		 * GoSD's kernel has no WLAN drivers for a card there anyway.
+		 */
+		status = "disabled";
 		bus-width = <4>;
 
 		vqmmc-supply = <&vdd_1v8>;
@@ -577,6 +596,23 @@
 		wakeup-source;
 	};
 
+	mmc@700b0600 {
+		/*
+		 * GoSD (github.com/jphastings/gosd): SDMMC4 is the eMMC on
+		 * the P3448-0002 module. Bus width and non-removable follow
+		 * mainline's Jetson TX1 module (tegra210-p2180.dtsi); the
+		 * supplies are the rails NVIDIA's DTS for this module names
+		 * (MAX77620 SD3 at 1.8 V, and VDD_3V3_SYS). Speed modes come
+		 * from tegra210.dtsi's SDMMC4 node, as on the TX1.
+		 */
+		status = "okay";
+		bus-width = <8>;
+		non-removable;
+
+		vqmmc-supply = <&vdd_1v8>;
+		vmmc-supply = <&vdd_3v3_sys>;
+	};
+
 	usb@700d0000 {
 		status = "okay";
 		phys = <&micro_b>;
